  (text_box "ToDo's:\n- switch to 4x D-Flip Flop wit Q and ~{Q}\n- use fixed quarz oszi with 32 kHz\n- use 4x D-Flip to devide down\n- exchange to 4x SPDT switch to change clock and DIR\n- add Silk Screen Labels for Qs and ~{Q}s on each IC pin\n- add header and extra optocoupler for Tacho Out with V_{IN}\n	-> w Signal, from active clock signal\n- add two Ground Posts for the Osci Clip\n- adjust via hole from Posts to tight fit\n- seperate opto supply to buffered DC/DC In Voltage\n- add 10-20 22uF Cs to this supply\n- exchange MosFet driver with dual ones in BGA package\n- switch two Mosfets of the same kind at once to save more space\n- reduce to one pcb, idealy only on top side\nDC/DC::\n- adjust undervoltage lockouts to 4V\n- adjust L to 10µH\n- change Vout to 1.8V\n	-> change Rv of Opto LEDs to 51R\n- remove Elko and place big ceramics\n- exchange power supply to 5V LDO and dual voltage regulator for negative supply -3.3V und +3.3V\n- 5V from LDO supplys VCCI on MosFet drivers\n- buffered 12V Voltage supplys VCCA/VCCB of MosFet drivers\nLOGIC:\n- checking if AND can be replaced with NANDs -> not possible/available\n- add TVS Diodes on the Flip Flops Inputs\n- series resistors for all inputs"
